{
 "name": "hatchback_car",
 "notes": "Concept layout of a small car (automobile, hatchback, saloon, sedan) with a front engine and rear drive, built from separate parts so it can be pulled apart, weighed and drawn. Front is +X, left is +Y, wheels on the ground at z = 0. The body is 23 thin panels from the car_body module (2.5 mm steel, 4 mm acrylic glazing); no part of it is a solid block. Powertrain: four cylinders in line with straight-shaft crank, rods, pistons and liners; a five-speed gearbox with ten spur gears that each have a keyway and backlash; a propshaft through a hole in the firewall; a rear differential whose crown wheel and pinion are drawn as spur gears for layout only (they would be hypoid). Simplifications: no valves, cam, crank throws, suspension arms, seats' frames, glass seals, lights or wiring; the sealed gearbox and diff cases have open tops; windows are acrylic. Not a crash-rated or road-legal design.",
